// APNT created-note seal, aggregate branch v0 (witness-index variant).
//
// Maturity: frozen — read by the frozen apnt_settlement_authorization_covenant_v0.ts;
// `npm run verify:settlement-authorization-covenant-independent` confirms this
// branch is exactly the witness-index variant that fits the 201-byte standard
// locking limit. See AGENTS.md, "The maturity ladder".
//
// Target architecture:
// openspec/changes/define-apnt-private-spend-covenant-v0/design.md
//   §1.1.6, as superseded by §1.1.6a's adopted decision.
//
// This is the aggregate half of a created note's seal. It delegates rather than
// duplicates: it does not verify a proof, does not check spend authority, and
// performs no transaction reconstruction. It requires only that a designated
// verifier input is present in this transaction, that the input really carries
// the deployment's pinned verifier token category, and that it is locked by the
// pinned settlement authorization covenant `L_verdict`.
//
// Everything else rides on that one input: the SAC at `L_verdict` requires this
// whole transaction to equal the projection committed in the verdict NFT, and
// the verdict NFT can only exist at `L_verdict` by having been threaded through
// a completed verifier run (design.md §1.1.2 property A).
//
// ADOPTED VARIANT: witness-index, not design.md §1.1.6's last-input script.
// §1.1.6 derived the verifier input index as `OP_TXINPUTCOUNT OP_1SUB`, which
// silently assumes that input is always last. Two of the four canonical
// statements (`private-split`, `private-split-flat-aggregator-service-fee`)
// place it at index 2, so that script cannot spend seals created under them
// (design.md §1.1.6a correction 6). This variant takes the index from the
// seal's own unlocking bytecode instead and is correct at any index.
//
// This is sound despite the spender choosing the index: whichever index is
// named must still carry the pinned category AND be locked by the pinned
// `L_verdict`, so it must be a genuine verdict input, and that input's own SAC
// binds this entire transaction.
//
// Expected witness stack on entry:
//   [ designatedVerifierInputIndex ]
//
// The pinned category constant is substituted by the TypeScript builder into
// the verifier-category marker below, and MUST be in VM byte order — reversed
// relative to the JSON/RPC representation (design.md §1.1.2, confirmed by
// measurement).
//
// The pinned category is a bare 32 bytes, which by OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY's own
// specification matches ONLY an immutable, non-minting NFT: a mutable or
// minting token pushes the category concatenated with a capability byte (33
// bytes) and will not compare equal. The chunked verifier's terminal token must
// therefore be immutable (design.md §1.1.6a correction 7).
//
// This is a locking-template artifact. It is not APNT acceptance, lane
// advancement, note spendability, proof verification, or broadcast approval.

// --- duplicate the witness-supplied verifier input index ---
OP_DUP

// --- require that input's token category to be the pinned C_verifier ---
OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY
@VERIFIER_CATEGORY_PUSH@
OP_EQUALVERIFY

// --- require that input to be locked by the pinned L_verdict (the SAC) ---
OP_UTXOBYTECODE
@VERDICT_LOCKING_PUSH@
OP_EQUAL
